CSS keywords. engine.s parses eight
declarations--width, height, float,
font-style, font-weight, font-family,
margin-top, margin-bottom--and skips
everything else in silence.
width, float and height are status-area
only: see the bar above, and keys 0-7.
---
Margins. The only part of this page the
automated backends render.
[before 2em + 3em]


Two blank lines above, three below.



[after 2em + 3em]
[before 2ch + 2en]
Two above and two below on the 6502, none on the JS engine, whose frontend
parses only 'em'. The two gold files must differ here.
[after 2ch + 2en]
[before relative]
Relative margins are rejected outright, not read as 50. Nothing above or below.
[after relative]
[before unknown declarations]
Five unknown declarations, then a margin-bottom: 1em that still works--one blank
line below, none above.

[after unknown declarations]
